{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running an automated \"stitch\" task (#5491) from a code generation pipeline. The task requires implementing four SRD requirements for `cmd/sha384sum`:\n   - **srd075 R2.1**: `--check FILE` must read FILE, parse each line (GNU or BSD tag format), recompute the SHA-384 digest, and compare to the stored hash.\n   - **srd075 R2.2**: Must print \"FILENAME: OK\" or \"FILENAME: FAILED\" for each entry. Must exit 1 if any check fails.\n   - **srd075 R2.3**: `--warn` prints a warning for each malformed line. `--quiet` suppresses OK lines. `--status` suppresses all output.\n   - **srd075 R3.1**: `-b` marks input as binary; output uses \"HASH *FILENAME\". `-t` (default) uses \"HASH  FILENAME\".\n   \n   Design decisions mandate using `pkg/hashutil.VerifyChecksums` and `pkg/hashutil.CheckOptions` (no reimplementation), and extending the existing main.go without restructuring.\n\n   Acceptance criteria: AC1 (compiles), AC2 (go vet passes), AC3 (all four requirements implemented), AC4 (no regressions to R1.1-R1.4), AC5 (no duplicated logic from pkg/hashutil).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - SHA-384 checksum computation using `crypto/sha512.New384`\n   - GNU checksum format: `HASH  FILENAME` (text) or `HASH *FILENAME` (binary)\n   - BSD tag format: `SHA384 (FILENAME) = HASH`\n   - Check mode verification via `pkg/hashutil.VerifyChecksums`\n   - `pkg/hashutil.CheckOptions` struct for `Warn`, `Quiet`, `Status` flags\n   - `pkg/hashutil.HashConfig` struct with Algorithm, NewHash, DigestLen fields\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils`\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd075-sha384sum.yaml**\n     - Contains all requirements R1-R4 for sha384sum\n     - R2.1-R2.3 define check mode behavior, R3.1 defines binary/text mode flags\n     - Non-goals: no HMAC-SHA384, no SHA-512\n     \n   - **cmd/sha384sum/main.go** (file to modify)\n     - Already contains a complete implementation from the previous R1.1-R1.4 task\n     - **Critical finding**: The existing code already appears to implement ALL four target requirements (R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R3.1)\n     - Check mode (R2.1, R2.2): Lines 24-41 handle `opts.check`, creating `hashutil.CheckOptions` and calling `hashutil.VerifyChecksums`\n     - Warn/quiet/status (R2.3): Lines 25-29 populate `CheckOptions{Warn, Quiet, Status}`; `parseArgs` handles `--warn`, `--quiet`, `--status` flags (lines 94-96) and `-w` short flag (line 113)\n     - Binary/text mode (R3.1): `-b` sets `opts.binary=true`, `-t` sets `opts.binary=false` (lines 83-86, 107-109); passed to `hashutil.DigestFiles` on line 42\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     package main\n     import (\n         \"crypto/sha512\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/hashutil\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         opts, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         cfg := hashutil.HashConfig{Algorithm: \"SHA384\", NewHash: sha512.New384, DigestLen: 48}\n         if opts.check {\n             checkOpts := hashutil.CheckOptions{Warn: opts.warn, Quiet: opts.quiet, Status: opts.status}\n             exitCode := 0\n             for _, f := range files {\n                 ok, err := hashutil.VerifyChecksums(f, cfg, checkOpts, os.Stdout, os.Stderr)\n                 if err != nil {\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"sha384sum: %s